<title>UK: Telstra 1.5 bln French franc bond due next week.</title>
<headline>Telstra 1.5 bln French franc bond due next week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's government-owned telecommunications company Telstra Corp is due to issue a 1.5 billion French franc 10-year bond next week, syndicate managers said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The deal was expected to be priced to yield in the mid-20s basis points over OATs. Banque Nationale de Paris and J.P. Morgan are joint lead managers.</p>
<p>The transaction will be the first French franc issue by an Australian borrower.</p>
<p>The Australian government wants to sell a third of Telstra for about A$8.0 billion but is facing tough opposition.</p>
<p>-- Aline van Duyn, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7748</p>
